 			<p>“Oh, the little villain! that’s the way he meant to pay me for keeping my word to mother. I’ll give him a hearty scolding, and bring him over to beg pardon,” cried Jo, burning to execute immediate justice. But her mother held her back, saying, with a look she seldom wore⁠—</p>
 			<p>“Stop, Jo, you must clear yourself first. You have played so many pranks, that I am afraid you have had a hand in this.”</p>
